{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6c8b48289b550bf61cce907438d4dcefa003982c7ff040728cdf6a33a5dee491","digest":{"component_or_area":"adapters / jira integration / value maps","key_entities":["_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE","LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA","adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py","test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py","test_exactly_one_type_map_literal_within_adapters","test_outbound_differ_session_log_exclusion.py","LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA","LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate map literals","single-source","code duplication","boundary guard","ticket type mapping","divergence risk"],"propositions":["Two identical definitions of the ticket-type map literal exist in separate Cloud and DC adapter modules, creating divergence risk across deployments.","The boundary guard that prevents duplicate map literals for status and priority does not cover the ticket-type map, allowing future duplication to go undetected.","The canonical ticket-type map must be relocated to adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py and imported under the _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE alias in both adapters to maintain module-attribute resolution.","External consumers like test_outbound_differ_session_log_exclusion.py read _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE as a module attribute and must not be broken by the refactor.","The boundary guard must be extended to enforce exactly one ticket-type map literal under adapters/ and reject any reintroduced duplicates."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787681609309629001,"uuid":"91ca1aa1-ac36-49a8-9c93-